\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 2.3 Decoupling: ML Training Pipeline vs. UI Application\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 To guarantee immediate, zero-latency interactive performance inside Streamlit, model training and grid searches are designed to run offline (e.g., in Google Colab, as referenced by \cf5 \cb6 colab_export_results.py\cf2 \cb3  in the code comments) and exported as static tabular files in \cf5 \cb6 /results/\cf2 \cb3 :\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf5 \cb6 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
results/manifest.json\cf2 \cb3 : Defines schema versions, parameters, and partition dates.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf5 \cb6 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
results/forecast_metrics.csv\cf2 \cb3 : Holds test performance scores for all 48 model-feature-target runs.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf5 \cb6 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
results/forecast_predictions_all.csv\cf2 \cb3 : Holds all 2,496 individual monthly predictions.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf5 \cb6 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
results/energy_vs_behavioural.csv\cf2 \cb3 : Stores ablation delta comparisons.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The user interface dynamically consumes these baked results for inspection, while \cf5 \cb6 modules/forecasting_models.py\cf2 \cb3  contains the complete, self-sufficient code allowing another researcher to retrain the models from source data.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 2.4 Interplay: Empirical Forecasting vs. Dynamic Simulation\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Forecasting Pipeline: An empirical machine-learning architecture evaluated out-of-sample on historical data (test window: 2021\'962025) using observed past features.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Simulation Sandbox: A forward-looking structural engine (\cf5 \cb6 modules/abm_simulator.py\cf2 \cb3 ) that accepts user-defined parameter overrides (        \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ) and simulates synthetic policy counterfactuals (e.g.,         \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
       bps rate shock) over a 24- to 48-month horizon using theoretical decay equations.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
