\cf2 \cb3 17. Validation and Diagnostic Mechanisms\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The project incorporates multiple validation layers across econometric, ML, and simulation modules:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 17.1 Machine Learning Validation\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls42\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Strict Out-of-Sample Split: 52 contiguous, unseen test months (January 2021 to April 2025).\cb1 \
\ls42\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Rolling Time-Series Cross-Validation: 5-fold forward-chaining \cf5 \cb6 TimeSeriesSplit\cf2 \cb3  on training data to prevent temporal look-ahead during hyperparameter selection.\cb1 \
\ls42\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Multi-Metric Assessment: Simultaneous tracking of scale-dependent metrics (RMSE, MAE), scale-independent variance explained (        \
\ls42\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ), and direction-of-change accuracy (MDA).\cb1 \
\ls42\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Leakage Isolation: Separation of leakage-free models (\cf5 \cb6 AR-only\cf2 \cb3  and \cf5 \cb6 Energy+AR\cf2 \cb3 ) from models incorporating ABM-derived look-ahead features (\cf5 \cb6 Energy+Behavioural+AR\cf2 \cb3  and \cf5 \cb6 Full\cf2 \cb3 ).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 17.2 ABM Structural Validation\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls43\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Heuristic Performance Comparison (
\f2\b \cf5 \cb6 msfe_comparison
\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb3 ): Tabulates historical MSFE, RMSE, and relative MSFE between fundamentalist and trend-following forecasts.\cb1 \
\ls43\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Rolling Accuracy Stability: Tracks temporal shifts in 12-month rolling MSFE to verify that heuristic dominance shifts coincide with known macroeconomic volatility regimes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 17.3 Econometric and Data Validation\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stationarity Transformations: Automated first-differencing in VAR models to ensure series stationarity.\cb1 \
\ls44\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Information Criterion Lag Selection: AIC automated lag-order selection (\cf5 \cb6 select_order(maxlags=12)\cf2 \cb3 ), bounded by available sample degrees of freedom.\cb1 \
\ls44\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Hypothesis Testing:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Welch's two-sample         \
\ls44\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      -test (\cf5 \cb6 scipy.stats.ttest_ind\cf2 \cb3 ) evaluating whether macroeconomic indicators differ significantly between energy-shock and normal months.\cb1 \
\ls44\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Granger causality Wald tests (        \
\ls44\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      -test and         \
\ls44\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      -value) testing predictive precedence of fuel prices on inflation.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls44\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Two-Sample Correlation & Rank Checks: Computes both parametric (Pearson         \
\ls44\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ) and non-parametric (Spearman rank) coefficients alongside         \
\ls44\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      -values for GVA transmission regressions.\cb1 \
