How to read heatmaps ("Red indicates a fall; blue indicates an increase").\cb1 \
\ls46\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
How to interpret RMSE ("Measures the typical size of forecast errors; lower is better").\cb1 \
\ls46\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What an energy shock represents ("Only the largest 10% of monthly price increases").\cb1 \
\ls46\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What an impulse response curve represents ("Estimates how an unexpected shock to one variable is followed by changes in others").\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls46\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
