\cf2 \cb3 20. Project Limitations\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 20.1 Explicitly Documented Limitations (from code, comments, and manifest)\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls47\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
ABM Look-Ahead Leakage: As explicitly disclosed in \cf5 \cb6 results/manifest.json\cf2 \cb3 , the ABM used \cf5 \cb6 fuel.shift(-1)\cf2 \cb3  as the target price in calculating forecast errors, introducing mild look-ahead into the historical rolling MSFE. (Mitigated partially in the ML pipeline by an additional lag).\cb1 \
\ls47\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Retail Forecastability: The out-of-sample         \
\ls47\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
       values for Retail Sales are negative across all models and feature sets, documenting that monthly retail volume changes were essentially unforecastable during the volatile 2021\'962025 period.\cb1 \
\ls47\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stationarity Constraints: Raw macroeconomic series exhibit strong non-stationarity and unit roots, requiring differencing in VAR models, which eliminates low-frequency equilibrium relationship information.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 20.2 Implementation Observations (Directly observable from the code)\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls48\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Small Sample Size: The historical dataset contains only 263 monthly observations (2003\'962025). Splitting at December 2020 leaves         \
\ls48\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
       training rows and 52 test rows, which severely limits the degrees of freedom for training high-capacity models like XGBoost and LSTM.\cb1 \
\ls48\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Absence of High-Frequency Energy Commodities: Fuel prices are represented solely by road pump prices (\cf5 \cb6 petrol\cf2 \cb3 , \cf5 \cb6 diesel\cf2 \cb3 ). Natural gas and wholesale electricity prices (which drove the 2022 UK cost-of-living crisis) are not present in the dataset.\cb1 \
\ls48\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Synthetic Policy Shock Decay: The shock propagation function in \cf5 \cb6 modules/abm_simulator.py:simulate_shock_response()\cf2 \cb3  imposes a hard-coded exponential decay curve (        \
\ls48\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ) rather than estimating dynamic response paths econometrically from the data.\cb1 \
\ls48\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tree Model Overfitting: HistGradientBoosting and XGBoost consistently performed worse than linear regularised models on GVA growth (RMSE         \
\ls48\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
       vs.         \
\ls48\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ), likely due to fitting noise in the small training sample.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
