\cf2 \cb3 The following items cannot be established or verified from the files provided in the workspace:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls52\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Standalone Literature Review Document: The Project Brief states a requirement for "Conducting a comprehensive literature review on economic crises, consumer spending behaviour, and relevant psychological factors". A standalone literature review document or chapter is not present in the workspace files.\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Specific External Data Source Citations & CDIDs: While column naming conventions match official UK ONS, BEIS, and Bank of England publications, formal data citations, series identifiers (e.g., ONS CDIDs), and exact revision dates for \cf5 \cb6 data/uk_macro_integrated.csv\cf2 \cb3  are not documented.\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
ARIMA and Prophet Models: The Project Brief specifies "predictive modelling approaches such as ARIMA, Prophet, and machine learning models (e.g. LSTM)". Neither ARIMA/SARIMAX nor Meta's Prophet model is imported or implemented in the Python files.\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Clustering & Advanced Anomaly Detection: The Project Brief lists "advanced data analytics techniques, including time series analysis, clustering, and anomaly detection". Beyond interquartile range (        \
\ls52\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      ) outlier detection on consumption and PCA dimensionality reduction, formal unsupervised clustering models (e.g., K-Means, DBSCAN) or anomaly detection algorithms (e.g., Isolation Forests) are not present in the code.\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Exact Currency / Value Units of Consumption: The column \cf5 \cb6 total_consumption_cvm\cf2 \cb3  is documented in \cf5 \cb6 analytics_engine.py\cf2 \cb3  as having level type, but whether its absolute values (e.g., 316,413.0 in June 2003) represent millions of pounds chained volume measure or an indexed base is not explicitly stated in the files.\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pre-Training of LSTM in Results Files: The script \cf5 \cb6 modules/forecasting_models.py\cf2 \cb3  contains a complete Keras implementation of an LSTM neural network, but LSTM results are absent from \cf5 \cb6 results/forecast_metrics.csv\cf2 \cb3  and \cf5 \cb6 results/forecast_predictions_all.csv\cf2 \cb3 .\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Causal Economic Transmission Mechanisms: The provided files demonstrate statistical associations, cross-correlations, regression fits, and reduced-form VAR impulse responses; they do not establish structural economic causality.\cb1 \
